sections.text:
gaddest—runnest to and fro, now
seeking help from Assyria (2Ch 28:16-21), now from Egypt (Jer 37:7, 8;
Isa 30:3).

full end—utter destruction: I will
leave some hope of restoration (Jer 5:10, 18; 30:11;
46:28; compare Le 26:44).

(Jer 12:15).

not pull … down … not pluck …
up—only partially fulfilled in the restoration from Babylon;
antitypically and fully to be fulfilled hereafter (Jer 32:41;
33:7).

scribe—one of the court secretaries;
often in the East part of the private house of a public officer serves
as a prison.

children—(Jer 39:6;
41:10). "wives …
children … thou"; an ascending climax.

watch over … for evil—(Jer 1:10;
Eze 7:6). The God, whose
providence is ever solicitously watching over His people for good,
shall solicitously, as it were, watch for their hurt. Contrast Jer 31:28;
32:41.

(See on Jer 49:26;
Jer 50:30; Jer
50:37).

plead … cause—(Jer 50:34).

sea—the Euphrates (Jer 51:13;
Jer 50:38). Compare Isa 19:5, "sea," that is, the Nile (Isa 21:1).

gave judgment upon him—as guilty of
rebellion and perjury (Jer 52:3;
compare Eze 23:24).
